# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: native-pipeline-yaml-not-linted -- an invalid rule in .gitlab/native.yml passes every repo check and silently kills the child pipeline
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: ci-infra
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-08

* Symptom

MR !462 (IntersectWith) added four probe jobs to =.gitlab/native.yml= with
=if: '$$MACOS_RUNNER == "online" && ...'= (a doubled =$=). GitLab rejects that
expression ("rule if invalid expression syntax"), so the parent's
=native:pipeline= bridge failed with =downstream_pipeline_creation_failed=
twice (pipelines 2925982648, 2926066881) and NO macOS / Windows job of that MR
ran -- not only the new probes, every native lane. The bridge's failure
reason says nothing about the YAML; the cause was only found by posting the
file to the project's CI lint API (=ci/lint= with the file as =content=):

#+begin_example
valid: False
ERROR jobs:intersectwith:probe:bricscad:macos:rules:rule if invalid expression syntax
...
#+end_example

=check-native-pipeline-changes=, =check-probe-families=,
=check-cad-sweep-gating= and =glab ci lint= (which lints =.gitlab-ci.yml=,
not the included child file) all passed.

* Fix

Lint =.gitlab/native.yml= itself in the repo checks: a script posting it to
the CI lint endpoint (needs a token -- fine in CI, optional locally), or an
offline check for the shapes GitLab rejects (a =$$NAME= in a =rules: if=,
unbalanced quotes / regex slashes). Run it in =check-native-pipeline-changes=
or as its own make target in the lint lane.

Fixed by hand in MR !462 (commit 89a9921e).
